<BaseLayout
  title="Hogwarts Legacy — Edition & Platform Guide"
  description="A buying guide for Hogwarts Legacy across PS5, Xbox, and Switch: edition differences, performance by platform, and where to buy cheapest."
>
  <article class="post">
    <h1>Hogwarts Legacy — Edition & Platform Guide</h1>
    <p class="meta">PS5 / Xbox / Switch · Updated 2026-08-05</p>

    <p>
      <strong>Hogwarts Legacy</strong> is the open-world Harry Potter action-RPG
      that lets you attend Hogwarts, learn spells, and explore the wider wizarding
      world in the 1800s.
    </p>

    <h2>Standard vs Deluxe Edition</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Standard</strong> — the full game, everything you need</li>
      <li><strong>Deluxe / Collector's</strong> — cosmetic packs and a few days early access; no story content</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The Deluxe extras are cosmetic only — Standard is the smart buy for most players.</p>

    <h2>Which platform?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>PS5 / Xbox Series</strong> — best visuals and load times</li>
      <li><strong>Switch</strong> — portable, but noticeably lower fidelity; fine for handheld fans</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where to buy cheapest</h2>
    <p>
      Hogwarts Legacy is now a mature title, and that's good news for buyers. Key and
      bundle stores clear older hits aggressively — Fanatical in particular runs
      site-wide events where back-catalog games like this drop 50% or more. Compare
      against console-store sales before you commit.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to buy</h2>
    <ul class="buy-list">
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="fanatical"
          href="https://www.fanatical.com/en/search?search=hogwarts+legacy"
          cta="Check Fanatical"
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="amazon"
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Hogwarts+Legacy"
          cta="Check on Amazon"
        />
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note">
      Prices change frequently — always verify on the store before purchasing.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

